## 7. Optional
`npm install` is NOT needed to run the system. The front-end libraries are already
copied into `assets/vendor/`. Only run it if you want to refresh those copies from `node_modules`.

## How the code is organized
Every request goes through `index.php`:

    Browser -> index.php -> Router -> Controller -> Model -> Database
                                          |
                                          +-> View (display only)

- `controllers/`  read input, check login, CSRF and permissions, then pick a view. No HTML, no SQL.
- `models/`       all SQL and validation (PDO prepared statements).
- `views/`        display only. `views/layout/` holds the shared header, sidebar and footer.
- `core/`         shared classes: Router, Session, Csrf, Model, BaseController, Nav.
- `config/`       app settings and database connection.
- `assets/`       css, js, and vendor libraries (Bootstrap, DataTables, jQuery).
- `database/`     schema.sql and seed.sql.

## Troubleshooting
- "could not find driver": step 5 was skipped.
- Apache "Not Found" page: check the URL starts with `/BOOTH/` and `BASE_URL` is correct.
- Blank styling: hard-refresh with Ctrl+Shift+R.
- Database errors are logged to `storage/logs/app.log`.
